125:     - Grey path forms a one-stroke trail under 8-connectivity; its start/end cells touch exactly two destination sprites via ports.
126: 
127:     Rule:
128:     - Destination sprites are determined by the grey trail's two endpoints.
129:     - For each destination, find the source sprite whose border color equals the destination's center color.
130:     - Replace the destination's center pixel with the source's center color.
131:     - Delete all non-destination sprites; grey paths and destinations remain.
132: 
133:     Key insight: Center color of each destination acts as a lookup key into the border colors of other sprites, enabling indirect color transfer.
134:     """
